  m_Text: This is an Oil Spill. The Florida Everglades are at risk from large bodies
    of oil that wash up in and smother newly laid eggs. This contaminates the water,
    vastly diminishing their living conditions. It has the potential to kill a multitude
    of fish as well as the mangroves which lay root in these waters.
